It's clear that you've never tried. 

>From Eva Myers' pets spoiler: 

>> Polymorphing yourself into a female egg-laying monster and laying an
>> egg is a useful technique for acquiring pets. 

This strongly suggests that any egg you've laid yourself will hatch into
a pet. (And my experience confirms that; I've had snakes, killer bees,
spiders, naga hatchlings, gargoyles and several different baby dragons
as pets from eggs I laid)

>> You can also sometimes 
>> get pets from eggs which you didn't lay, although this is probably
>> less useful. Any dragon egg which hatches while you are carrying it
>> will become a tame baby dragon. 

That is, whether or not you've laid it yourself, and whether you're male
or female. You only need to be carrying it when it hatches (but that
goes for all eggs, including those you've laid yourself).

>> If you are male, any egg at all which 
>> hatches while carried by you has a 50% chance of yielding a pet.
>> (From the source code, ``The identity of one's father is learned, not
>> innate''.) 

I can't tell from this if it includes eggs you laid yourself while you
were a female egg-laying monster, or just applies to eggs you've picked
up and aren't generic 'eggs' but <monster> eggs.

